{"content":"💡 **SUGGESTION: connector segments stop short of the node — visible line→dot gaps**

The `::before` connector is sized `left: -50%; width: 50%`, so it spans from the previous node's center to **this step's left border**, not to the dot at the step's center. Zooming the regenerated fixture (`factory-board.visual-check.1440x900.dark.png`) shows the gaps clearly: each line ends half a step-width before the next dot, so the strip reads as `dot ─── gap ○` rather than a connected track.

The fix is one property — widen the pseudo-element to full step width so it terminates under the dot (the dot paints over it, since it renders after the pseudo in the same stacking context):

```css
.step::before {
  content: ''; position: absolute; top: 4px; left: -50%; width: 100%;
  height: 2px; background: var(--line-2);
}
```

(`width: 100%` spans `-0.5w → +0.5w`, i.e. previous center → this node's center; for pending dots with a transparent fill the line showing through behind the outline is fine and actually improves the connected look. If it ever glints, add `position: relative` to `.step-dot`.)

The state-color semantics (connector takes the target node's color, so the line into a done node is green) are good — this is purely the geometry.
","path":"outputs/pr_review_comments/comment1.md"}

{"content":"💡 **SUGGESTION: silent fallback when `steps.js` fails to load**

```javascript
var steps = (window.FACTORY_STEPS || { stepStates: function () { return []; } })
  .stepStates(c, laneId);
if (!steps.length) return '';
```

If `steps.js` ever 404s or throws during load (bad deploy, cache skew, ad-blocker edge case), every card silently loses its status strip — the exact feature this PR exists to deliver — with no signal anywhere. `index.html` loads the scripts in the right order and the unit suite pins the contract, so this is belt-and-braces only, but a one-time warning makes the degradation diagnosable:

```javascript
if (!window.FACTORY_STEPS) {
  (console.warn || function () {})('factory board: steps.js not loaded — card status strips disabled');
}
```

Alternatively fail loud (`throw`) if you'd rather the board show its error state than render cards without strips — your call; either is better than silent.
","path":"outputs/pr_review_comments/comment2.md"}
